  with plain commands only (`git commit -F <msg> --only -- <paths>`, one per commit; no shell functions, loops or
  heredocs). Build the end state: no "owed" item inside this mandate survives to the hand-back.
bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road.mem:69:# The tw5 plugin bundle (`packages/lararium-tw5/plugins/lares-memetic-wikitext.json`, `plugins/standalone/*`, `src/plugin-tiddler.generated.ts`) rides in git and must equal a fresh build: rebuild after any tw5 source or tiddler change and commit it with the change. CI's `build-freshness` job checks it. `genesis/` carries that bundle, the boot shadows and the engine blob by address, and the wiki inside a founded vessel runs the bytes genesis carries; a bake (`pnpm --filter @lararium/node build:genesis`) lands as its own labelled `GENESIS RE-BAKE` commit with the CAS change, and a vessel founded on the earlier seed re-founds. `tools/genesis-parity-witness.sh` reads the gap: a bundle that runs ahead of genesis reads red until a bake closes it or a row in `genesis/unbaked.json` declares it.
bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road.mem:99:* ''The fence'' (operator ruling, 2026-10-16). Early alpha runs while one or two operators hold the mesh and ends when a third human's data and habits enter it; after that, data deserves a migration path. The second operator takes the seat beside the first as a QA tester who knows the mesh stays a sandcastle until then. As practice, not law, the destroy-class and shape-changing acts land before the second seat where they can: the engine re-mint and the genesis re-bake; the carrier and key-class changes; the Stable re-found (AID, charter, seat); every signed-shape change; every load-bearing rename.
bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road.mem:208:* ''Custody and identity read by capability, never by host'' (operator ruling, 2026-10-19: //"I consider node and browser isomorphic-by-intent. Eventually, a browser-vessel somewhere may grow comparable capabilities to a node vessel, and this pattern cascades outwards to all future vessels."//). Three rules hold on every vessel, present and planned: a vessel meets each face through that face's atom alone, its veil signing every dial, join, enrolment, sibling channel and daemon proof made on that face's behalf, never one device-wide key; a vessel holds a place signer exactly while it stands a floor, for the floor's allowlisted duties, under the pre-rotated place KEL; and a faceless vessel reading another's floor proves nothing private, reading the public shelf under the floor card's pin. A node's daemon auth, device-key signer, sibling enrolment and group-secret opener read the one vessel seed today (`open-node-vessel.ts`), and a browser's do the same (`open-browser-vessel.ts`); each is a bond owed, carried by `K15`.
bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road.mem:214:* ''One owner per registry; the floor reads by CID'' (operator ruling, 2026-10-18: //"Architecture stands, leans stand"//). The `@oracle` document as a registry every vessel writes retires: one id carried one `lares` and one `lararium` pointer for the whole fleet, and a joined vessel's pointer replaced its hearth's, a shape a two-vessel probe and three shard runs measured. `@oracle` stands as the floor's read-face over a manifest CID, which a wiki mounts read-only by the pin its face accepted. Each registry carries only what its scope's owner writes: a vessel's bootstrap holds its own document pointers and its accepted floor pins; `@catalog` the operator's documents; the Kahu realm the live `lares` and `lararium` documents and their drafts; the crossroads board the Nexus's one public answer. The leans the ruling adopts: the Kahu realm holds the live system documents, with `bags/` projected on the Kahu's vessel alone; a one-seat founding lands a counted 1-of-1 Kahu-cabal admission for persona zero's group, so one predicate decides every hand's reach into system canon; the release answer, the Nexus's one public answer, names the Nexus AID, the charter epoch, the release before it and the floor manifest CID, sealed by the steward, with the promotion approval over the manifest's exact bytes riding attached; a vessel records an accepted release as a sealed hot row per (face, Nexus) that only a person's act moves; genesis bakes the first floor, a corpus CID in the seed. A signing domain of its own carries the release, `floor-release`, so no seal over another shape verifies as one (operator-approved, 2026-10-18). The shape and its slices stand at <<~ loulou "lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/pono/w26-floor-lane">>; rows `W26`, `W21` and `P8` carry the build.
bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road.mem:224:* ''The disk watcher's reach'' (house ruling under the operator's delegation, 2026-10-14). A pending removal settles with no person present only under a standing instruction the operator signs by a human route, naming one bag and a bounded class of removals (a path pattern and a per-wave count ceiling): the watcher executes within it, every settled removal lands in the audit with the instruction it rode, and `lares shore restore` still answers it. An automated seat never signs one, a standoff (disk and records differ) never settles without a person, and a mass vanish past the instruction's ceiling stays pending for a person. The reason: a person who answered in writing for exactly that class has answered, and a count alone proves no intent; the ruling flips on a single incident where an in-scope instruction deleted what a person meant to keep (<<~ loulou "lar:///ha.ka.ba/lararium/api/disk-projection#/projection-law">>).
bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road.mem:244:* ''The floor announcement'' (house ruling under the operator's delegation, 2026-10-15). `waking-floor-announce` signs one canonical body per carried Nexus under that Nexus's floor bundle signing key: version, Nexus AID, floor route pin digest, floor standing and causal position. It travels only inside an authenticated socket or relay relation. The reader checks the already pinned floor pin, domain, Nexus, route and causal order, and treats the body as a peer hint alone. The reason: a floor hint must neither bootstrap its own trust nor replay across Nexuses. The ruling flips on a smaller body that still refuses cross-Nexus replay, stale replacement and first-contact self-certification.
bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road.mem:248:* ''The channel of intent'' (operator, 2026-10-20: //"Approve your leans, land the full models into the architecture now"//). The daemon wiki keeps working memory; a face's intents travel on that face's own intent plane, `@intents-<tag>`, a fifth face plane beside the four; a vessel's own records rest in its daemon bag, unmirrored; the face's pins rest in the face's custody and `@persona`. The approved leans: the plane stands from the first landing, never staged in the daemon bag; the winner reads by the intent's own preference list, else the lowest `H(atom ‖ intent id)`, and never elects; a single-effect fleet-wide verb never addresses "any device", and a human answer may name its executor; a claim never expires, a device's staleness stays a local suspicion, and the operator's release always wins; an `every` intent reaches a later-joined device unless its bound names a roster edge; a far agent reaches the plane through a relay seat, opt-in per face and ring-gated, its research before its build; an intent voids by supersession, a revoked delegation, a passed roster edge or the operator's cancel; compaction folds by the operator's act, never a timer; a local verb that touches its own vessel alone bypasses the plane and leaves its receipt in that vessel's bag. The plane carries a hand's decisions that cross devices, never its motion (the rubric, <<~ loulou "lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/face-intent-plane">> #/the-rubric). Row `I1`.
bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road.mem:326:* The R-ENGINE fold target dependency line, in fixed order: automerge-repo and its four listed adapters at alpha.5 → `@automerge/automerge` 3.4.1 → `@keyhive/keyhive` 0.3.0-alpha.1; no Subduction or Onomancy dependency → the genesis re-bake (`GENESIS_ENGINE_CID`, every fixture holding the hearth true-name, the untracked CAS in the same commit) → the fold's own live proof on the rebuilt image, with a pushed shard run reading green. The manifests hold all three dependency steps (`packages/lararium-node/package.json`, `packages/lararium-keyhive/package.json`); a Keyhive Archive and a cap event carry no format tag, so bytes one Keyhive version wrote refuse under another and a version move re-founds every vessel. The fold's own live proof on the rebuilt image stands owed.
bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road.mem:338:* ''The hosting rows'': a hearth's hosting state, each spend and its walkers' carriage rest as HOT rows sealed under the S key, in the storage home of the custody seat (`packages/lararium-node/src/hosting-store.ts`, `hosting-carry.ts`). The sealed writer writes a whole file and appends to none, so each spend lands as ONE row of its own, named by a digest of its nonce or marker: the row's presence IS the burn, and it reads, decides and seals under one custody holder. The spend row commits a redemption, and what rides ahead of it re-derives: the grant from the epoch, the leaf, the nonce and the claim, so a crash before the answer replays as `retry`; the operator's counts from the rows standing, by name. A roll's state row commits the roll, and the hosting doc re-derives from it: the next roll and each sovereign stand land an act the sealed state holds and the doc lacks (`landHostingActs`). The sweep of dead epochs' rows passes through the seat's removal door (`removeCustodyRow`), which removes only a row this vessel's key opens; a spend that sealed after a roll retired its epoch burns nothing live and leaves with the next sweep. Each carried value rests as one row whose name carries its address and its length, so a guest's bytes read off its rows and no counter stands beside them. One process serves a hearth's carriage (the standing vessel's own gate, under its store claim), and its contacts and deposits run in turn, so a quota reads the bytes the last deposit left and a reclaim never discards on a reading a contact moved meanwhile. A row that stands and does not open refuses by name: a burn nobody can read never reads as unspent, and a carried value nobody can open never reads as absent. A floor composition reads no hosting row, so a locked hearth sorts no socket as a walker. `lares host`, `host roll` and `host invite` ride the custody door (`host.state` · `host.roll` · `host.invite`): a minted invite as a verb's outcome would rest in the daemon's document in the clear.
bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road.mem:459:* `K15` One hive per face (#/rulings, 2026-10-18): each PersonaGroup owns its Keyhive identity, event store, registry, archive and content-key seat, and no identity stands above them. Build order, each step red-first: (0) before bytes move, the custody contract of <<~ loulou "lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/pono/k15-custody-step-zero">>: the node and browser row census sorted D, F or S, the FCK key class, each face's own slot tree and recovery route, the carrier binding of face, row name and kind, and the overwrite contract generalized to a row-class key (#/rulings, a face's custody rows seal under its own key; a shared act never makes a shared secret) (the node census built, PR #70: each carrier row names its target classes, a LEAD mark and its open joint, and `encodeCarrierContext` spells the D and S seal context; the archive-row-selector joint traced and held open, PR #71: no archive site hands its row an authenticated PersonaGroup); (1) a substrate probe that two Keyhive instances in one process hold apart under interleaved acts, a reboot and a cross-read (measured: isolation holds, `packages/lararium-keyhive/tests/two-hives-one-process.probe.test.ts`), then a face context with its own store, registry, archive and key seat; (2) the face as the sole owner of its identity and group, the vessel's delegation gone from every face-bearing event (built, PR #68: `makeFaceBagDoor`, `faceOwnerVerifier`, a two-face event-byte capture its red, `W25`'s probe its regression), and 2b, a bag keeping one Document across boots (built, PR #68: `registerBagsDurably`, its record on the daemon doc for the vessel's ground and on each face's plane for that face's bags); the door grants the face's group before it records a Document (PR #69), so a crash between them re-enters to the same end; (2c, operator ruling 2026-10-19; built, PR #79) the atom cut: a random atom per (vessel, PersonaGroup) under that face's FCK signs every act on the face's behalf on node and browser, the place signer keeps the floor's duties alone, the wire subjects and verifiers move together, and its genesis, admit and founding-bootstrap deltas ride `X0` by `genesis/unbaked.json`, red-first on a thief holding the place seed deriving no veil and opening no group secret; on the local presence channel the session wears the mounted face, so a verb's presenter derives from the island's own atom and never from the CLI's unsigned `requestedBy`, the floor presents the place for floor acts alone, and a verb that names another face refuses by name (#/rulings, a session wears the face, 2026-10-11; a published atom key would link face and vessel on a wire); (3) sessions and registries routed by one face, no union, with `F6` slice three's asker-seals beside it, each sealer holding its row class's key (built, PR #81: the browser house keys by (PersonaGroup, persona root), the island proves each face through `gate:clear` while the holder holds no key, the island reads the fleet board's dyad itself, a fresh group mints a fresh atom, founding seeds key by their ask digest, and the node keys its atom and veil-archive rows by PersonaGroup digest; the daemon's last unions ride step 6); (4) content keys and removal per face, `K12`'s fresh group inside it; (5) a one-face restore and a herm that carries yet authors nothing; (6) the fence migration, identity bytes, split stores, slot trees and FCKs, and archive and custody formats together, under one identity model (#/rulings, sync carries, verification decides: the sealed anchor, the signed `@persona` log, verified projections): each D row (the atom's seed, its archive) seals under its face's FCK, where the node now seals them under the seated vessel key, and keys by its PersonaGroup, as the node's atom and veil-archive rows and the browser's atom row already do, where the browser's veil archive still keys by handle index. The isolation red: unlock face A alone, bypass every route, and try to open and replace B's occupied carriers with every key A holds, the S key included; each open fails, B's bytes stand unchanged, and A's bundle restored on a fresh vessel holds nothing of B. Lead: DreamNet-Wright after `W26`'s floor slice lands. K, W. Wave C (step 6 under the identity anchor, `readFace` as the one door with its census) landed in PR #86 on 2026-10-23. `K15-H` (the Handle owner rides the anchor, the row in `docs/pono/k15-wave-c-lane`) landed in PR #88. Wave D (the FCK fence, its eight slices whole, kit `docs/pono/k15-wave-d-lane`) landed in PR #95 on 2026-10-26: each face seals its D rows under its own FCK, unlocks apart, bundles and restores alone, lifts its anon veil on join, and seats when its grant arrives. `K17`'s realm leg (`docs/pono/k17-realm-lease-lane`) landed in PR #97 on 2026-10-26.
bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road.mem:487:* `I1` The face intent plane (#/rulings, the channel of intent, 2026-10-20; <<~ loulou "lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/face-intent-plane">>). Build order, each step red-first: `@intents-<tag>` minted by the PersonaGroup with its entry kinds (intent, outcome, asks and answer, claim, release and takeover, supersede and cancel), each signed by its device's atom and its id a content hash; stand-down and the three verb classes, with a single-effect verb addressed to "any device" refused at issue; the read-side winner; causal voids and the operator's release; the face-join summons moving off the daemon doc onto the plane, which closes two hearths of one face, beside the CLI naming its face per invocation; the daemon wiki's view pane; the rubric's witness (a hundred keystrokes and a save write no entry; one move writes one intent and one outcome); then the far agent's relay seat after its own research. Its reds stand at the carrier's #/the-reds. Its authority reads stand on the face's sealed identity anchor, so it builds after Wave C lands the anchor (operator, 2026-10-20, approving the controller's lean); the relay seat's own research wave follows it. Lead: a Sonnet Episkopos with a Sol and a Copilot seat. I. Built, PR #99, 2026-10-26 (kit `docs/pono/i1-intent-lane`): `@intents-<tag>` stands as the fifth face plane, registered by a signed `plane` act and never projected to disk; each entry signs under its own domain over the signed-act image, the intent id hashing issuer, verb, arguments and nonce; a device stands down on an answered slot, a single-effect verb addressed to a class or "any device" refuses at issue and an unpinned one waits on an `asks` gate whose `answer` names the atom; the winner reads by preference, then the lowest `H(atom ‖ intent id)`, with every duplicate kept visible; claims, takeover and causal voids read no clock, a finite `every` names a roster act on `@persona` and waits while its reader lacks it, and the persona root, the face's operator key, signs the release that outranks a claim; the face-join summons rides the face's plane (`lares intent issue|show|ask|answer|claim|takeover|release|cancel|supersede --face N`), the daemon-doc verb retired, and the effect door fences the pinned hearth and the operation id before any re-key, so a second hearth refuses and a replay returns its grant; the daemon wiki shows intents through a read-only pane; the rubric witness reads a seeded duplicate before trusting its zero. The far agent's relay seat stays out, after its own research.
bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road.mem:539:* ''Integrity owed: the habit flip at the bake'' (`X0`, `G37`). Before the bake the house runs re-genesis freely, since no CRDT document survives; after it, a re-genesis costs every CID a second operator pins. Its witness: a census of each instrument, fixture, brief and runbook line that assumes a free re-genesis, each named to flip or retire inside the bake's own commit, never after it.
bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road.mem:543:* `G15` The refold's answers. For the compose owner, who holds `open-node-vessel.ts`: `after-roll-awaited.test.ts` reads source shape alone, and wants the chain lifted into a module a vector can run; an unbounded `afterRollChain` stage can stall later rolls, and a bound must never let two refolds of one holder overlap. Beside those: the plugin build's transcript records a fixed logical path for the TW5 binary, never the resolved one (`build-plugin-tiddler.ts`); its cure moves genesis attestation bytes, so it rides a labelled re-bake. G.
bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road.mem:545:* `X0` The founding bake: one deliberate re-genesis before a second operator stands, after which CIDs are meant to last because another operator pins them. It moves together `K15` step 6 (identity bytes, split stores, slot trees and FCKs, archive and custody formats, each face's random device veil), the place KEL's pre-rotation and the scoped place signer (the signer frames each duty's domain itself, signing `len(D) ‖ D ‖ preimage` and its verifiers the same, so no signed floor image carries its own separation; built with `W29`, whose readiness red reads a fresh genesis founded armed, the five framed pairs verifying, and an old-shape inception refused by name, `old-shape-inception`), `W26`'s closing bake (the floor release), and `G37`'s preimage and format renames (`engine/v1` and its kin, the floor announcement's kind, the genesis seed and CAS formats). Each member carries its own readiness red, so the bake waits on the slowest by name, never on a date; the bake's own red: a fresh genesis founds, no CID from before the bake verifies after it, and a mixed old archive refuses by name. The gate it opens: a second operator may found a Nexus fresh at two of two. X.
bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road.mem:595:* `F8` The control-event leg stands built: `lar:control-event` and `lar:control-result` replace `wiki:dom-event` and `wiki:dom-input` (`lar-camera.ts`, `projection-sink.ts`). Owed to the o-takiage: burned-name guard assertions in `lar-wire.test.ts` and `projection-input-leg.test.ts`. O1.
bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road.mem:605:* `X0b` The idempotent-by-intent pass, after the founding bake, paralleling the isomorphic-by-intent law (operator, 2026-10-19): a replay, a reboot and a retry land nothing new. Every row names itself by its content or its causal id, never a clock or a counter; every write reads first-writer-wins or merges by its CRDT; every boot reads as a function of its stores; and every multi-step act either completes or re-enters to the same end. Its instrument: N boots, each Archive replayed twice, each verb retried, and the second pass of each adds no head and no row. Each finding before the bake cures as its own bug; its instrument runs once before the bake as a census beside `G37`, so a finding that renames a persisted row lands inside the bake, and this pass sweeps what remains. X.
bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road.mem:701:# The seed carries no version: a labelled genesis re-bake (`b96d68895`).
